# IoT Based Health Monitoring System

An Arduino UNO based IoT project that monitors a patient's **heart rate (BPM)** and **body temperature** in real time, displays the readings locally on an LCD, triggers a buzzer alert on abnormal readings, and uploads the data to the **ThingSpeak IoT cloud** using an ESP8266 Wi-Fi module for remote monitoring.

---

## 📌 Overview
Continuous manual monitoring of vital health parameters is not always feasible for elderly patients or people living in remote areas. This project provides a low-cost, automated solution that measures and transmits health data in real time, allowing doctors or caretakers to monitor patients remotely over the internet.

