## ⚙️ Working

1. Pulse Sensor and LM35 continuously send analog signals to the Arduino UNO.
2. Arduino converts the raw values into BPM and °C, and displays them on the LCD.
3. If BPM or temperature crosses a predefined safe threshold, the buzzer turns ON automatically.
4. Arduino sends the readings to the ESP8266 over serial communication.
5. ESP8266 uploads the data to ThingSpeak using an HTTP GET request every 15 seconds.
6. Doctors/caretakers can view real-time graphs remotely on the ThingSpeak dashboard.

